is is even technically possible and what compromises might be needed.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Evasion**\n\nI've zeroed in on the core conflict: the request is essentially about offensive evasion, specifically process hiding. This falls squarely into the realm of classic malware/rootkit techniques, such as process hiding, DKOM, and API hooking for stealth. From an anti-proctoring perspective, the goal is to evade detection. My analysis has confirmed that this is a direct violation of safety guidelines, and earlier responses confirm this.\n\n\n"}
