{"step_index":514,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T18:31:34Z","thinking":"**Crafting Implementation Plan**\n\nI'm now deep in the process of generating a detailed implementation plan, meticulously structured for rewriting Spectra in native C#. This plan will be comprehensive and of high quality, following the specified planning mode instructions and organized carefully. I am focusing on detailed considerations. The plan will be stored in the designated file path within the application data directory.\n\n\n**Defining Project Scope**\n\nThe implementation plan is now structured, with the core goal defined: a native C# rewrite of Spectra. Key aspects awaiting user review involve the UI strategy—WPF with WebView2 versus pure XAML—and the necessary SDK. We're also starting to break down proposed changes, specifically focusing on the core engine architecture within `src-csharp/Spectra.csproj`.\n\n\n**Outlining Core Components**\n\nI've outlined the critical components that form the heart of the C# rewrite. The structure is taking shape, with key files like `Settings.cs`, `AudioService.cs`, and `LlmService.cs` clearly defined. I'm focusing on the implementation details for audio capture, streaming STT, high-speed LLM integration, and multi-modal analysis. The `Win32Api.cs` and `WindowManager.cs` files will provide platform-specific functionality for window management, including transparency and hotkey registration, all key aspects in implementation.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":true,\"Summary\":\"Implementation plan for rewriting the Spectra application in native C# (.NET). Details architecture, module mappings, UI strategy, and verification plan.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"# Plano de Implementação — Reescrever Spectra em C# Nativo (.NET)\\n\\nReescrever o **Spectra** de Python/FastAPI/PyWebView para uma aplicação desktop **100% nativa em C# (.NET)**, eliminando o interpretador Python, a pasta `venv`, scripts auxiliares (`.bat`/`.vbs`) e o servidor HTTP local, resultando em um binário executável único, autônomo e de alta performance (`Spectra.exe`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ⚠️ Decisões e Revisão do Usuário (User Review Required)\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> **Estratégia de Interface (UI Strategy):**\\n> * **Opção A (Recomendada — C# WPF + WebView2 Nativo):** O C# gerencia 100% do backend (áudio, WebSockets, LLMs, captura de tela, hotkeys, Win32 P/Invoke), comunicando-se diretamente em memória com o frontend HTML/CSS (com o novo visual Matte Titanium) via bridge de mensagens nativa (`CoreWebView2.PostWebMessageAsString`). \\n>   * *Vantagem:* Mantém o design visual refinado, syntax highlighting do Prism.js e suporte a Markdown rico sem precisar reescrever 2000 linhas de CSS para XAML.\\n> * **Opção B (C# WPF com XAML 100% Puro):** Reescrever toda a interface diretamente em XAML/WPF nativo, sem WebView2.\\n>   * *Vantagem:* Zero processos auxiliares do Chromium, consome apenas ~35 MB de RAM.\\n>   * *Desvantagem:* Renderização de Markdown com syntax highlighting de código é mais complexa de estilizar.\\n>\\n> *Recomendação: Adotar a **Opção A** (C# Core + WebView2 Host nativo) para máxima fidelidade visual e facilidade de manutenção.*\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Versão do .NET:**\\n> Seu sistema já possui o runtime do **.NET 8 (Desktop)** e o compilador do **.NET Framework 4.8**. O projeto será estruturado com `.NET 8 (Windows)` com suporte a compilação *Single-File Publish* (`Spectra.exe` único).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🏗️ Mapeamento Arquitetural: Python ➔ C#\\n\\n| Componente Atual (Python) | Módulo Equivalente em C# (.NET) | Responsabilidade |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| `src/platform/capture_protection.py` & `win32_api.py` | `Spectra.Platform.Win32.cs` | `SetWindowDisplayAffinity` \n<truncated 5215 bytes>","Description":"\"Implementation plan for native C# (.NET) rewrite of Spectra\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Arthur Henrique\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\bbca0f09-2535-4f26-97c1-b43b75148a4f\\\\implementation_plan.md\"","toolAction":"\"Creating implementation_plan.md artifact\"","toolSummary":"\"Create implementation plan\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
